"1\n00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,229\nThe Learning Brain. Series 3: Generative AI\n\n2\n00:00:06,100 --> 00:00:07,340\nEpisode 4\n\n3\n00:00:07,420 --> 00:00:09,269\nCrutch or tutor\n\n4\n00:00:12,069 --> 00:00:17,162\nNearly a thousand high school students practised maths with one of two AI tutors,\n\n5\n00:00:17,371 --> 00:00:19,348\nor with no AI at all.\n\n6\n00:00:19,852 --> 00:00:22,420\nOne tutor was a standard chat interface.\n\n7\n00:00:22,760 --> 00:00:24,698\nThe other was prompted to give hints,\n\n8\n00:00:24,824 --> 00:00:25,915\nnot answers.\n\n9\n00:00:26,085 --> 00:00:28,609\nDuring practice, both helped a lot.\n\n10\n00:00:29,136 --> 00:00:33,514\nThe standard chat raised scores by forty eight percent over the control group.\n\n11\n00:00:34,067 --> 00:00:38,138\nThe hint giving tutor raised them by a hundred and twenty seven percent.\n\n12\n00:00:38,308 --> 00:00:41,170\nThen the AI was taken away for the exam.\n\n13\n00:00:41,670 --> 00:00:48,710\nStudents who had practised with the standard chat scored seventeen percent lower than students who never had AI.\n\n14\n00:00:49,182 --> 00:00:53,556\nStudents from the hint giving tutor scored about the same as the control group.\n\n15\n00:00:53,726 --> 00:00:55,487\nThe logs suggested why.\n\n16\n00:00:55,880 --> 00:00:59,787\nWithout guardrails, many students used the AI as a crutch,\n\n17\n00:00:59,986 --> 00:01:02,158\nasking for the answer and copying it.\n\n18\n00:01:02,628 --> 00:01:05,194\nThe effort that builds skill never happened.\n\n19\n00:01:05,364 --> 00:01:08,881\nThis is the testing and generation effects from Series two,\n\n20\n00:01:09,063 --> 00:01:10,467\nrun in reverse.\n\n21\n00:01:10,872 --> 00:01:15,160\nRetrieval and generation build lasting memories because they take effort.\n\n22\n00:01:15,590 --> 00:01:17,183\nGetting the answer is easy.\n\n23\n00:01:17,548 --> 00:01:19,485\nProducing it is what teaches.\n\n24\n00:01:19,655 --> 00:01:20,448\nA caution.\n\n25\n00:01:20,940 --> 00:01:22,098\nThis was one school,\n\n26\n00:01:22,118 --> 00:01:25,267\none subject, about fifteen percent of the curriculum,\n\n27\n00:01:25,313 --> 00:01:27,473\nwith a model from twenty twenty three,\n\n28\n00:01:27,720 --> 00:01:29,828\nand the students were in high school,\n\n29\n00:01:29,869 --> 00:01:31,040\nnot university.\n\n30\n00:01:31,521 --> 00:01:33,967\nAnd the safeguarded tutor prevented harm,\n\n31\n00:01:34,166 --> 00:01:36,589\nbut did not raise exam scores.\n\n32\n00:01:36,759 --> 00:01:37,527\nFor teaching.\n\n33\n00:01:37,892 --> 00:01:40,247\nIf students use AI in practice,\n\n34\n00:01:40,425 --> 00:01:43,194\ngive them a tutor that hints rather than solves.\n\n35\n00:01:43,593 --> 00:01:46,113\nGrade the process, not just the answer.\n\n36\n00:01:46,462 --> 00:01:49,344\nAnd always include some unassisted practice,\n\n37\n00:01:49,489 --> 00:01:52,452\nso you and they can see what they can do alone.\n\n38\n00:01:52,622 --> 00:01:55,174\nAI can carry students through the practice,\n\n39\n00:01:55,371 --> 00:01:56,917\nor make them do the climbing.\n\n40\n00:01:57,312 --> 00:01:59,245\nOnly one builds the skill.\n\n"
